The intent of the CERT Advisory was not to encourage system operators to
read users' e-mail.  The message was simply, if a site's policy is to
allow the monitoring of keystrokes, a warning banner should be displayed.

CERT encourages all sites to create a site specific computer security 
policy.  What is covered by the policy is up to each site.  Monitoring users
(it is okay or it isn't okay) should be covered in this policy.  If your
site doesn't have a policy, check out RFC1244.  This RFC can be found at
your local RFC anonymous FTP site.  It is also available via anonymous
FTP from cert.org in the pub/ssphwg directory.

If you're unhappy about the site's policy, talk it over with the computing 
facilities managament.  They will hopefully be able to explain how and
when monitoring will occur.  This would be a more effective approach than
posting to Usenet.

